    mechanic: 2
    hintText: Yangjiang douchi should use the Large amount. It should remain the strongest savory flavor.
  - ruleId: L10_Hint_CoarseSalt_Ratio
    priority: 21
    mechanic: 2
    hintText: Coarse salt should use the Very Small amount. It should bring out the other flavors without tasting salty.
  - ruleId: L10_Hint_Douchi_Order
    priority: 22
    mechanic: 1
    hintText: Start with Yangjiang douchi. Its deep savory flavor needs time to form before the other ingredients arrive.
  - ruleId: L10_Hint_Ginger_Order
    priority: 21
    mechanic: 1
    hintText: Ginger should come after douchi and before dried tangerine peel.
  - ruleId: L10_Hint_Tail_Order
    priority: 20
    mechanic: 1
    hintText: Add dried tangerine peel near the end, then add coarse salt last.
